# Data Gap Report — Structured Per-Source Response
> Responding to Ammar Sohail's requirements doc  
> Numbers computed live from `CustomerDataMasterVerse.xlsx` (312,658 rows)

---

## 1. Data Completeness Summary — Per Source

| Source | Records | Unique Phones | % Name | % City | % Email | % Address |
|--------|--------:|-------------:|-------:|-------:|--------:|----------:|
| **Exhibition** | 109,180 | 109,162 | 31% | 100% | 0% | 0% |
| **JobBox** | 67,986 | 67,986 | 97% | 100% | 0% | 0% |
| **OE** | 47,825 | 47,825 | 26% | 100% | 25% | 100% |
| **Changan** | 33,065 | 33,065 | 100% | 100% | 0% | 0% |
| **CFH** | 21,828 | 21,828 | 100% | 100% | 2% | 100% |
| **POS** | 15,708 | 15,708 | 0% | 100% | 0% | 99% |
| **Others** | 17,066 | ~17,000 | ~varies | 100% | ~0% | ~varies |

**"Others" breakdown:** DuraFoam (5,106) · MasterOffisysView (4,516) · Dealers (4,072) · DDS (3,335) · MoltyHome (37)

> **What this tells us about identity strength:**
> - **JobBox / Changan / CFH** — strong identity data (name + phone always captured), but **zero email** → can be reached by phone only
> - **Exhibition** — 69% missing name → mostly anonymous footfall; phone is the only identifier
> - **POS** — 0% name in Excel (names are stored in the live POS API, not the Excel snapshot)
> - **OE** — weakest name capture (26%) but has **25% email**, the only channel with meaningful email coverage

---

## 2. What Each Historical Source Represents

| Source | What This Source Likely Represents |
|--------|-----------------------------------|
| **Exhibition** | Footfall / leads captured at MasterGroup trade shows and exhibitions. Customers who visited a stall, expressed interest, or gave their phone for a follow-up. **No purchase record implied** — these are leads, not confirmed buyers. |
| **JobBox** | CRM / lead management system records. Customers who interacted with a sales agent, placed an inquiry, or were registered in the CRM pipeline. May or may not have converted to a sale. |
| **OE** | Online Express — Shopify-based e-commerce orders placed on the MasterGroup website. Each row = a confirmed online purchase. Has the richest data (address, partial email, order items). |
| **Changan** | Partnership sales via the MasterGroup × Changan automotive partnership. Customers who bought a Changan vehicle and were offered MasterGroup products (e.g., car cushions, seat accessories). Each row = a Changan-channel customer interaction. |
| **CFH** | Celeste Home Fashion — home décor / bedding brand under MasterGroup. Customers who purchased from CFH retail, likely through a separate POS or dealer system. Each row = a CFH transaction or registered customer. |
| **POS** | Point of Sale — in-store and dealer transactions recorded at MasterGroup retail counters. Walk-in customers; names not captured in this Excel snapshot (captured separately in the live POS system). |
| **Others** | Internal system snapshots: `DuraFoam` (Dura Foam brand contacts), `MasterOffisysView` (internal ERP/office system view), `Dealers` (registered dealer accounts), `DDS` (dealer distribution system), `MoltyHome` (MoltyHome brand contacts). Mostly B2B / channel partner records. |

---

## 3. Data Quality Issues — Per Source

| Source | Key Data Issues (Historical Excel) | Key Data Issues (API / Live System) |
|--------|------------------------------------|--------------------------------------|
| **Exhibition** | **69% missing names** — walk-in footfall only gives phone. No address. No email. Phone format inconsistent (10-digit without `+92` prefix). | N/A — not in API |
| **JobBox** | Very good identity data (97% name, 100% phone). **Zero email** — CRM didn't capture email. Phone normalization needed (`3xxxxxxxxx` → `+923xxxxxxxxx`). | N/A — not in API |
| **OE** | **74% missing names** in Excel snapshot (online orders often use first name only or alias). 75% missing email in Excel. However the live OE API fills these gaps significantly. | Phone format inconsistency (11-digit `03x` vs 10-digit `3x`). Province blank for smaller cities. Duplicate province names (`Islamabad` vs `Islamabad Capital Territory`). |
| **Changan** | **100% name and phone** — clean partnership data. Zero email, zero address. Only 33K records but high completeness. | N/A — not in API. No order/product data available. |
| **CFH** | **100% name and phone**, 2% email only. 100% address — physical address captured. No product/purchase data in Excel. | N/A — not in API (separate Celeste POS system likely exists) |
| **POS** | **0% name in Excel** — names exist in live POS system but were not included in this Excel export. 99% address coverage is misleading — it's dealer address, not customer address. | `brand_name` always `"-"` (19% of all DB orders). Product IDs inconsistent: some numeric (`77263`), some slugs (`Molty-Spring-78-66`). Dummy phone `03000000000` used for anonymous walk-ins. `order_status` always `"completed"` — no cancellations or returns tracked. |
| **Others** | Mixed quality. `Dealers` records are B2B (company name, no individual). `MoltyHome` has only 37 records. `DDS` likely reseller channel. | N/A — not in API |

