## 4. Source-Level Relevance for Recommendations

| Source | Current Use for Recommendations | Missing Data to Improve |
|--------|--------------------------------|------------------------|
| **OE** | ✅ **Full personalization** — collaborative filtering, SVD, product pairs, content-based similarity. Full purchase history available (176K orders). | Acquisition channel attribution (how customer found us). 75% email gap limits email-based campaigns. |
| **POS** | ✅ **Full personalization** — 113K orders used for all ML algorithms. Higher avg order value (PKR 52K vs OE PKR 24K). | Product categories not captured (`product_type = "simple"` — unusable). Brand always blank. Returns/cancellations not tracked. |
| **Exhibition** | ❌ **Generic only** — 109K customers receive only popularity-based fallback suggestions. No purchase data exists. | Need: which exhibition leads converted to buyers (phone match). If conversion data provided, we can link ~30-50K leads to real purchase history. |
| **JobBox** | ❌ **Generic only** — 68K CRM leads receive only popularity fallback. No purchase data. | Need: CRM purchase records or order history per phone. Even `(phone, product, date, amount)` would unlock personalization for this segment. |
| **Changan** | ❌ **Generic only** — 33K Changan customers have no MasterGroup purchase data. Massive missed cross-sell opportunity (car owner → car cushions, ergonomic products). | Need: Changan order records. Known product affinity: car accessories → MoltyFoam / ergonomic crossover. |
| **CFH** | ❌ **Generic only** — 22K CFH customers invisible to engine. Home décor purchase signals could enable home-comfort cross-sell. | Need: CFH sales records. CFH → Celeste home bedding → MoltyFoam sleep products is a natural cross-sell path. |

